Select the best translation into predicate logic. Some firefighters rescue victims from danger. (Dx: x is danger; Fx: x is a firefighter; Vx: x is a victim; Rxyz: x rescues y from z)
A. (∃x){Fx • (∀y)[Dy ⊃ (∃z)(Vz • Rxyz)]}
B. (∃x){Fx • (∃y)[Vy • (∃z)(Dz • Rxyz)]}
C. (∃x){Fx • (∃y)(∃z)[(Vy • Dz) • Rxzy]}
D. (∀x){Fx ⊃ (∃y)[Vy . (∃z)(Dz • Rxyz)]}

An ant crawls straight from $(-4,6)$ to the origin, and then continues straight on to $(4,3)$. How far does it travel?
A. 16
B. 2\sqrt{2}
C. 5
D. 5+2\sqrt{13}

What is the inverse of $f(x)=4-5x$?
A. \frac{5}{x-4}
B. \frac{x-4}{5}
C. \frac{x+4}{5}
D. -\frac{x-4}{5}

We roll a fair 6-sided die 5 times. What is the probability that we get a 6 in at most 2 of the rolls?
A. \frac{125}{648}
B. \frac{25}{648}
C. \frac{625}{648}
D. \frac{1}{648}
